1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,196
The stent is in.

2
00:00:01,521 --> 00:00:03,379
What happens after the cath lab?

3
00:00:04,191 --> 00:00:08,986
Recovery includes an access-site check, a
medicine plan and follow-up for the heart

4
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:10,739
condition that led to treatment.

5
00:00:11,343 --> 00:00:16,231
PCI is a catheter procedure that treats a
narrowed heart artery.

6
00:00:16,742 --> 00:00:21,340
Afterward, staff check your blood pressure
and pulse and look for bleeding where the

7
00:00:21,386 --> 00:00:26,471
catheter entered. The access site, the way
it was closed and your condition all

8
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:28,758
affect when you can get up and go home.

9
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:34,261
After a stent, your team usually
prescribes antiplatelet medicines.

10
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:39,532
They make platelets less likely to clump
together and form a clot inside the stent.

11
00:00:40,229 --> 00:00:45,314
The plan depends on why you had PCI, your
chance of bleeding and any other

12
00:00:45,372 --> 00:00:50,248
medicines you take. Your discharge summary
should tell you which plan applies to

13
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:50,874
you.

14
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:56,157
Before you leave, confirm which medicines
are new and whom to contact about side

15
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:57,910
effects or missed doses.

16
00:00:58,514 --> 00:01:02,902
If another clinician plans surgery or
dental work, tell them about your stent

17
00:01:02,983 --> 00:01:08,324
and your medicines. Your care teams can
work together before any medicine change.

18
00:01:08,928 --> 00:01:14,233
Your own discharge instructions cover the
dressing, activity, lifting, driving and

19
00:01:14,315 --> 00:01:19,017
return to work. A small bruise or mild
tenderness can occur.

20
00:01:19,342 --> 00:01:24,287
Increasing pain, redness, swelling,
drainage or fever are reasons to

21
00:01:24,369 --> 00:01:25,878
contact the care team.

22
00:01:26,389 --> 00:01:30,917
How quickly you can return to activity
depends on your recovery and the reason

23
00:01:30,975 --> 00:01:31,846
for treatment.

24
00:01:32,449 --> 00:01:37,395
Get emergency help for severe chest pain,
sudden trouble breathing, heavy bleeding

25
00:01:37,465 --> 00:01:40,530
or bleeding that will not stop at the
access site.

26
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:46,381
A hand or foot that suddenly becomes cold,
pale or numb on the side

27
00:01:46,555 --> 00:01:49,005
used also needs urgent attention.

28
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:54,647
Your discharge plan should identify whom
to call with other concerns.

29
00:01:55,344 --> 00:01:59,721
The treated section is only one part of
coronary artery disease.

30
00:02:00,417 --> 00:02:04,539
Follow-up gives your team a chance to
check symptoms, review medicines and

31
00:02:04,585 --> 00:02:06,408
discuss the prevention plan.

32
00:02:07,011 --> 00:02:12,062
Cardiac rehabilitation can provide
supervised exercise, education and support

33
00:02:12,178 --> 00:02:13,594
when it is appropriate.

34
00:02:14,105 --> 00:02:16,241
Your team can tell you how to join.

35
00:02:16,752 --> 00:02:21,408
Before you leave, ask for the treatment
result, the written medicine and recovery

36
00:02:21,478 --> 00:02:25,239
plan, and a clear contact for follow-up or
problems.

37
00:02:25,843 --> 00:02:30,336
A planned procedure and an emergency
procedure can lead to different recovery

38
00:02:30,406 --> 00:02:34,272
plans. Keep the plan that your team gives
you.
